  "issue": {
    "id": "I_kwDOAd1its7g8iwi",
    "databaseId": 3773967394,
    "number": 1779,
    "title": "The releases have incorrect files ARM has x86 files and AMD has aarch64 files in packages",
    "url": "https://github.com/ros2/ros2/issues/1779",
    "body": "### Generated by Generative AI\n\nN/A\n\n### Operating System:\n\n```Ubuntu Desktop on Raspberry PI```\n\n### ROS version or commit hash:\n\nJazzy packages have incorrect lib \"so\" files. \n\n### RMW implementation (if applicable):\n\n_No response_\n\n### RMW Configuration (if applicable):\n\n_No response_\n\n### Client library (if applicable):\n\n_No response_\n\n### 'ros2 doctor --report' output\n\n<details><summary>ros2 doctor --report</summary>\n\n```console\n<COPY OUTPUT HERE>\n```\n</details>\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce issue\n\n1. Download ARM architecture file - \"ros2-jazzy-20250820-linux-noble-arm64.tar.bz2\" file from releases \n2. Untar or extract the files to the current directory - \n3. cd ros2-linux\n4. run command - find . -name \"*pybind*\" and you'll see x86_64 files in it. \n5. run command -  find . -name \"*aarch64*\" and you'll see not any files. \n6. Download AMD architecture file - \"ros2-jazzy-20250820-linux-noble-amd64.tar.bz2\" file from releases \n7. Untar or extract the files to the current directory \n8. cd ros2-linux\n9. run command - find . -name \"*pybind*\" and you'll see aarch64 files in it. \n10. run command -  find . -name \"*x86_64*\" and you'll see not any files. \n\nThe package name is incorrect and/or the files are swapped. \n\n### Expected behavior\n\n1. Download ARM architecture file - \"ros2-jazzy-20250820-linux-noble-arm64.tar.bz2\" file from releases \n2. Untar or extract the files to the current directory - \n3. cd ros2-linux\n4. run command - find . -name \"*pybind*\" and you'll see aarch64 files in it. \n5. run command -  find . -name \"*aarch64*\" and you'll see current library files. \n\n### Actual behavior\n\n1. Download ARM architecture file - \"ros2-jazzy-20250820-linux-noble-arm64.tar.bz2\" file from releases \n2. Untar or extract the files to the current directory - \n3. cd ros2-linux\n4. run command - find . -name \"*pybind*\" and you'll see x86_64 files in it. \n5. run command -  find . -name \"*aarch64*\" and you'll see not any files. \n6. Download AMD architecture file - \"ros2-jazzy-20250820-linux-noble-amd64.tar.bz2\" file from releases \n7. Untar or extract the files to the current directory \n8. cd ros2-linux\n9. run command - find . -name \"*pybind*\" and you'll see aarch64 files in it. \n10. run command -  find . -name \"*x86_64*\" and you'll see not any files. \n\n### Additional information\n\nThe package names are incorrect ",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Generated by Generative AI</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">N/A</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Operating System:</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Ubuntu Desktop on Raspberry PI</code></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">ROS version or commit hash:</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Jazzy packages have incorrect lib \"so\" files.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">RMW implementation (if applicable):</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>No response</em></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">RMW Configuration (if applicable):</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>No response</em></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Client library (if applicable):</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>No response</em></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">'ros2 doctor --report' output</h3>\n<details><summary>ros2 doctor --report</summary>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-text-shell-session notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"&lt;COPY OUTPUT HERE&gt;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">&lt;COPY OUTPUT HERE&gt;</span></pre></div>\n</details>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Steps to reproduce issue</h3>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Download ARM architecture file - \"ros2-jazzy-20250820-linux-noble-arm64.tar.bz2\" file from releases</li>\n<li>Untar or extract the files to the current directory -</li>\n<li>cd ros2-linux</li>\n<li>run command - find . -name \"<em>pybind</em>\" and you'll see x86_64 files in it.</li>\n<li>run command -  find . -name \"<em>aarch64</em>\" and you'll see not any files.</li>\n<li>Download AMD architecture file - \"ros2-jazzy-20250820-linux-noble-amd64.tar.bz2\" file from releases</li>\n<li>Untar or extract the files to the current directory</li>\n<li>cd ros2-linux</li>\n<li>run command - find . -name \"<em>pybind</em>\" and you'll see aarch64 files in it.</li>\n<li>run command -  find . -name \"<em>x86_64</em>\" and you'll see not any files.</li>\n</ol>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The package name is incorrect and/or the files are swapped.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Expected behavior</h3>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Download ARM architecture file - \"ros2-jazzy-20250820-linux-noble-arm64.tar.bz2\" file from releases</li>\n<li>Untar or extract the files to the current directory -</li>\n<li>cd ros2-linux</li>\n<li>run command - find . -name \"<em>pybind</em>\" and you'll see aarch64 files in it.</li>\n<li>run command -  find . -name \"<em>aarch64</em>\" and you'll see current library files.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Actual behavior</h3>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Download ARM architecture file - \"ros2-jazzy-20250820-linux-noble-arm64.tar.bz2\" file from releases</li>\n<li>Untar or extract the files to the current directory -</li>\n<li>cd ros2-linux</li>\n<li>run command - find . -name \"<em>pybind</em>\" and you'll see x86_64 files in it.</li>\n<li>run command -  find . -name \"<em>aarch64</em>\" and you'll see not any files.</li>\n<li>Download AMD architecture file - \"ros2-jazzy-20250820-linux-noble-amd64.tar.bz2\" file from releases</li>\n<li>Untar or extract the files to the current directory</li>\n<li>cd ros2-linux</li>\n<li>run command - find . -name \"<em>pybind</em>\" and you'll see aarch64 files in it.</li>\n<li>run command -  find . -name \"<em>x86_64</em>\" and you'll see not any files.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional information</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The package names are incorrect</p>",
